# Component Patterns and Guidelines

## Component Types

### Card Components
- [reusable_card.dart](mdc:lib/components/reusable_card.dart) - Contains multiple card variants:
  - `ReusableCard` - Basic card with color and onPress
  - `ReusableCard2` - Enhanced card with elevation, gradient, and rounded corners
  - `ReusableCard3` - Message card variant

### Content Components  
- [icon_content.dart](mdc:lib/components/icon_content.dart) - Icon with label layouts:
  - `IconContent` - Standard icon with text below
  - `IconMsgContent` - Icon with text and message counter badge

### UI Components
- [appbar_header_text.dart](mdc:lib/components/appbar_header_text.dart) - App bar title styling
- [list_tile.dart](mdc:lib/components/list_tile.dart) - Custom list tile implementations

### WebView Components
- `webview/navigation_controls.dart` - WebView navigation controls
- `webview/stack.dart` - WebView stack management
- `webview/webview_screen.dart` - WebView container

## Component Design Principles

### 1. Reusability
- Components should be generic and configurable
- Use required parameters for essential properties
- Provide sensible defaults where possible

### 2. Theme Consistency
- Always use `Theme.of(context).colorScheme` for colors
- Respect user's theme preferences
- Use consistent spacing and typography

### 3. Responsive Design
- Components should adapt to different screen sizes
- Use flexible layouts with `Expanded`, `Flexible`
- Test on various device sizes

## Common Component Pattern
```dart
class MyComponent extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyComponent({
    Key? key,
    required this.title,
    this.onTap,
    this.color,
  }) : super(key: key);

  final String title;
  final VoidCallback? onTap;
  final Color? color;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final theme = Theme.of(context);
    
    return Container(
      decoration: BoxDecoration(
        color: color ?? theme.colorScheme.surface,
        borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),
      ),
      child: Material(
        color: Colors.transparent,
        child: InkWell(
          onTap: onTap,
          borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12),
          child: Padding(
            padding: EdgeInsets.all(16),
            child: Text(
              title,
              style: theme.textTheme.bodyLarge,
            ),
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

## Animation Integration
- Use `flutter_animate` for component animations
- Common patterns: `.animate().fadeIn().scale()`
- Keep animations subtle and meaningful

## Accessibility
- Provide semantic labels for screen readers
- Ensure sufficient color contrast
- Support keyboard navigation where applicable

## Testing Considerations
- Components should be easily testable in isolation
- Minimize external dependencies
- Use dependency injection for services
